    "verdict": "Every pandas rolling(...) call in build_matrix is on a groupby(code) Series without a shift(-n), so the window is [t-w+1, t]. The only forward-looking arithmetic in the module is in the `label_*` section, which is what a target is supposed to be. min_periods = max(2, w//2) means short-history rows get NaN or a partial-window statistic; they are never back-filled from the future."
